    "body": "Horizon Harness 1.0.2\n\nIncludes the complete 1.0.1 update flow and a proxy compatibility fix:\n\n- Check for stable updates on every installed startup; click the version indicator or use `/update` to review, skip, or confirm.\n- Update through the original npm, Homebrew, or curl channel, then restart on success after closing the TUI and local service.\n- Show the working directory beside the model and the version at the bottom right; fix the update dialog's extra inner border.\n- Fix Windows directory hints and transient installer file locks.\n- Bundle SOCKS proxy support, including `socks5h`, and keep failed background checks silent. The native self-test now constructs a SOCKS transport to verify the packaged dependency.\n\n**Existing 1.0.0 / 1.0.1 installations:** upgrade once using the original package manager to obtain this fixed updater. API keys, sessions and settings remain in the user data directory.\n\n```sh\n# npm — macOS / Windows x64\nnpm install -g horizon-harness@1.0.2\n\n# Homebrew — macOS\nbrew update\nbrew upgrade 01ny-yzx/tap/horizon\n\n# curl — macOS\ncurl -fsSL https://github.com/01ny-yzx/horizon-harness/releases/latest/download/install.sh | sh\n```\n\nNative bundles include Python. Supported targets: macOS Apple Silicon, macOS Intel, and Windows x64.\n",
