    "published_at": "2026-11-03T22:25:09Z",
    "body": "**Superseded by [1.0.2](https://github.com/01ny-yzx/horizon-harness/releases/tag/v1.0.2):** the newer release fixes SOCKS proxy support for update checks.\n\nHorizon Harness 1.0.1\n\n- Check for stable updates in the background on each installed startup.\n- Use `/update` or click the version indicator to review, skip, or confirm an update.\n- Update through the original npm, Homebrew, or curl installation channel, then restart automatically after success.\n- Shut down the TUI and local service before installation; npm updates run from the Node launcher so Windows can replace the native files.\n- Show the working directory next to the model and the Horizon version at the bottom right.\n- Fix the extra inner border in the update dialog.\n- Normalize Windows home-directory hints and retry transient installer file locks.\n\n**Upgrading from 1.0.0:** run one of the commands below once to obtain the built-in updater. API keys, conversations, and settings remain in the user data directory.\n\n```sh\n# npm — macOS / Windows x64\nnpm install -g horizon-harness@1.0.1\n\n# Homebrew — macOS\nbrew update\nbrew upgrade 01ny-yzx/tap/horizon\n\n# curl — macOS\ncurl -fsSL https://github.com/01ny-yzx/horizon-harness/releases/latest/download/install.sh | sh\n```\n\nNative bundles include Python. Supported targets: macOS Apple Silicon, macOS Intel, and Windows x64.\n",
